Vaccines go through extensive clinical trials involving thousands of participants to assess safety and efficacy before approval.
Regulatory bodies such as the FDA and WHO enforce strict guidelines to ensure vaccines meet high safety standards.
Post-market surveillance systems continuously monitor vaccines for rare adverse reactions, ensuring ongoing safety.
The benefits of vaccination in preventing diseases far outweigh the minimal risks, as supported by extensive global health data.
Similar rigorous testing is applied to other medical treatments, reinforcing the reliability of vaccine safety protocols.